    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.dag_longest_path_length - EdgeCase\",\n    \"isPartOf\": {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.dag_longest_path_length.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.dag_longest_path_length()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get the length of the longest path in a directed acyclic graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.dag_longest_path_length()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Get the length of the longest path in a directed acyclic graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.dag_longest_path_length()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: >-\n  Get the length of the longest path in a directed acyclic graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nGet the length of the longest path in a directed acyclic graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L72073-L72155){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.dag_longest_path_length()\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![DAG longest path length](../assets/graphs/dag-longest-path-length.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"The seven-node DAG with task durations on its edges. The longest path, B, D, F, G in the accent color, has total weight 3 + 4 + 2 = 9.0, which the card gives as the result; ignoring the weights, the longest path has 3 edges.\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe length of the path returned by `dag_longest_path()`: the number of edges on an\nunweighted graph (an `int`), or the total edge weight on a weighted graph\n(`Graph(weighted=True)`, a `float`). In a scheduling DAG with task durations as weights,\nthis is the shortest possible time to finish every task, however many run in parallel.\nOn an unweighted graph it equals the number of topological generations minus one.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [int | float]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   The longest-path length; `0` for a graph without edges.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If the graph is undirected or contains a cycle.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~dag_longest_path`) \n\n:   The nodes of the longest path.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThe longest path of this pipeline takes 15 time units, through the tests:\n\n::: {#2a178d7e .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph.from_edges(\n    [(\"fetch\", \"compile\", 3.0), (\"compile\", \"test\", 10.0),\n     (\"test\", \"package\", 2.0), (\"fetch\", \"docs\", 4.0),\n     (\"docs\", \"publish\", 1.0)],\n    directed=True,\n)\ngraph.dag_longest_path_length()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```\n15.0\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Where shortening a task pays off\n\n`project()` is the plan for opening a made-up café, with an arrow from each task to every\ntask that can't start until it's done, weighted by the days the first task takes. The\ncafé can open after 66 days at the earliest:\n\n::: {#89e3a5a4 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nec.project().dag_longest_path_length()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n66.0\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nGetting the permits in 5 days instead of 15 brings the opening 10 days closer. Training\nthe staff in 1 day instead of 5 saves only 2, since the health inspection, which takes 3\ndays, then holds up the opening:\n\n::: {#b802804d .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\npermits = ec.project().set_edge_attrs(\"weight\", 5, sources=[\"Permits\"])\ntraining = ec.project().set_edge_attrs(\"weight\", 1, sources=[\"Training\"])\n\npermits.dag_longest_path_length(), training.dag_longest_path_length()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(56.0, 64.0)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {#092d3599 .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ntraining.plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", highlight=training.dag_longest_path(), label_by=\"label\",\n    height=360,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-63cc1385:#d4d4d8;--ect-879b7ebc:#949497;--ect-b9f8de6d:#872d08;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-63cc1385:#3f3f46;--ect-879b7ebc:#2c2c31;--ect-b9f8de6d:#ae500f;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-li